Dropcarrier Version 1.0

What Is It?

Dropcarrier is a program written in Arexx for Cnet Amiga sysops running
version 1.98 and above. 

What Does It Do?

Ever get a user that logs on, types "WHO" and drops carrier? or people that
otherwise are just too lazy to type 'O!'? Well, Dropcarrier remebers it,
and after 3 times, it holds a grudge.... upon login the offender will get a
message that goes like this

You Have Hung Up On Me 3 Times...


   Now Its *MY* Turn

¼½¼¢®ðß°æßððçßNO CARRIER (you get the picture)

How Do I Install It?

1) Copy the 2 Arexx files checkdrop and dropedcar to your pfiles: directory
2) Make a directory called "pfiles:logoff"
3) In Line 62 Of BBSText, Add \#0pfiles:Checkdrop\ to the end of the line
so it looks something like this

\n1@ Cleared for logon\#0pfiles:checkdrop\\n1

4) In Line 80 Of BBSText, Add \#0pfiles:dropedcar\ to the end of the line
so it looks something like this

\n1Lost carrier.\#0pfiles:dropedcar\\n1

5) Watch With Glee


